{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And these are the names of the children of Israel, coming into Egypt: Jacob and his sons.</b> The three patriarchs were all called Israel, and here Scripture calls Isaac Israel, for it says that Jacob and his sons are the children of Israel — and if so, Isaac too is called by the name Israel. Abraham as well is called Israel, from what is written (Exodus 12:40): ״ומושב בני ישראל אשר ישבו במצרים שלשים שנה וארבע מאות שנה״. And you already know that the reckoning is from the birth of Isaac, and Scripture includes them all among the children of Israel; if so, then Abraham too is called by the name Israel. Therefore the Talmud called Esau an apostate Israel (ישראל מומר), as is stated in the first chapter of Kiddushin in the passage about a gentile who inherits his father by Torah law, because he was of the seed of the patriarchs yet did not walk in their ways."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:41.714545460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}